.DS_Store

# personal details
docs/athlete-context.md

# --- Athlete data: NEVER commit. The GitHub repo is public. ---
# Deny-by-default: EVERYTHING under athlete/ is ignored, and only the shared,
# non-personal parts are named back in. A new athlete folder is covered the
# moment it is created, and so is anything inside it — including a session
# export the phone share sheet dropped at athlete/ or athlete/<slug>/ instead
# of in logs/.
#
# Note `athlete/*` has NO trailing slash, so it matches files as well as
# directories. With a slash, a stray athlete/session-2026-08-01.json would be
# committable — which is precisely the mistake this rule exists to prevent.
#
# Do NOT replace this with a list of names like athlete/*/logs/. Naming the
# things to exclude means anything you did not think of is committed by
# default, in a public repo, permanently.
athlete/*
!athlete/.gitignore
!athlete/README.md
!athlete/skills/
!athlete/sources/
